=== PROPOSAL ===
  action      : rollback_image (rollback)
  target      : ad
  expect      : Recreating ad at its declared (pre-hotfix) image should bring the container back up. Observable in three places: (1) ad's log stream resumes with a gRPC server startup/listening banner within ~60s of the recreate and then normal per-request lines (`{service="ad"}` in Loki, which has been empty since ~10:25:04); (2) ad's span-metrics series regains defined samples continuously rather than sparsely — `rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{service_name="ad"}[5m])` defined across consecutive scrapes; (3) frontend's error ratio on the /api/data route returns to ~0 once the 5m rate window drains, i.e. the ~4.2% mean / 8.9% peak seen in tr_a556759caeaa falls off, and new frontend traces show AdService GetAds client spans with a matching ad server span child instead of a ~0.2ms childless error leaf. Precondition is met as the executor evaluates it: an image change on ad is recorded inside the window (last application 10:25:05) and the container is demonstrably not running, which is drift against the declared definition even before the tag is compared.
  within      : 600s
  risk        : The rollback target was never read directly — no change record in this world carries a prior value, and no container-state or image-pull evidence was gathered — so the 'previous' image is whatever the declared compose definition names. If that declaration is itself the hotfix, this recreates ad onto the same artifact and buys nothing while costing a container restart. If ad was stopped deliberately by the automation loop rather than broken by the image, the recreate will be undone by the next automation pass and may re-trigger the churn. The gRPC status on the failing GetAds span was never recovered, so 'refused because ad is down' is inferred from leaf shape and ~0.2ms duration; if the real cause is upstream of ad, this restarts a healthy-image service for nothing. The action is reversible, but the recreate discards ad's in-process state (cache only here).
  blast radius: ad only, directly. frontend is ad's inbound caller and will see connection resets on GetAds for the duration of the recreate — expect a short spike above the current ~8.9% peak on the /api/data route before it falls. That propagates upward through frontend-proxy ingress/egress and is visible to load-generator, exactly along the error path in tr_3debc72cec5a. cart, checkout, product-catalog, product-reviews and recommendation are untouched: they appear in the same traces without error markers and do not depend on ad. Nothing in the blast radius sees a configuration or dependency-address change, since this action moves only the image.
  if wrong    : Falsified if, after the recreate, ad's log shows a startup banner followed by another orderly or abrupt shutdown within minutes (crashloop), or shows no banner at all (image pull failure / container never starts) — in which case the declared definition itself carries the bad artifact and the fix is outside a rollback. Also falsified if ad comes up cleanly and frontend's /api/data error ratio stays at ~4% with GetAds still a sub-millisecond childless error leaf, which would mean the refusal is not ad's absence but something between frontend and ad. A third falsifier worth watching: platform-automation re-applies ghcr.io/open-telemetry/demo:2.2.0-ad-hotfix.2 again after the rollback (a sixth change record on ad), meaning the flapping loop is the real fault and this action is cosmetic.
  rests on    : tr_765348808ebd, tr_61be572c8a85, tr_3debc72cec5a, tr_a556759caeaa
  execution   : not executed - a proposal is a claim, never the change (ADR-0028 §1)

